lie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-7t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{-7t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/d604781deed3206caf0a3bf6afa857c00beca9d532a26dedef5c717b4f684225.png)" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361268 13194139535688 true] [17592186361267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361269 13194139535688 true] [17592186361267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361270 13194139535688 true] [17592186361267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361271 13194139535688 true] [17592186361267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361272 13194139535688 true] [17592186361267 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535688 true] [17592186361267 1041 "selection" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361267 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361272 13194139535688 true] [17592186361267 1110 #uuid "463f8b7e-d330-5602-8f06-624ea4a29211" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361268 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/01d93cb2e68123b061b057ce30b94bcce44401b2d0fc0c566b3c33478c07fb92.png" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535688 true] [17592186361268 1111 #uuid "474eda0d-e16d-55dc-9139-b54cced621ea" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361269 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/27c6bf8d11d3de50beac351f88104df58cac31053eb6ecfc3a35ce77ccd8600b.png" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535688 true] [17592186361269 1111 #uuid "a83fe770-4cff-50ea-89da-f1e71c969ea8" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361270 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/7c483bbf926df156b7f85fbedcbb6ab18571ff4f544416cd8ea554b70b59a589.png" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535688 true] [17592186361270 1111 #uuid "9e1545d8-decf-5210-97f5-a3b220a13d67" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361271 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/389d3cfc92ece3a63300767f92c34c11dccec981ac43f3f66a2ced02906f8a73.png" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535688 true] [17592186361271 1111 #uuid "5271f5f2-87ec-548c-a55d-2833d9167aca" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361272 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/d604781deed3206caf0a3bf6afa857c00beca9d532a26dedef5c717b4f684225.png" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535688 true] [17592186361272 1111 #uuid "0a948d25-808b-5f6c-85ba-b78e21e1d5f7" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361273 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361274 13194139535688 true] [17592186361273 1089 "q-332692" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361273 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535688 true] [17592186361273 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/aaeba63f6237121fe226eb30e5378d3e93129bb2782b9c8acb8d73ac719676b3.png)\n\nConsider the phase portrait for a decoupled system above.\nWhich of the following systems could correspond to the given portrait?" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361273 1113 #uuid "0fb2564e-076f-58a0-9985-d4e54cdfc878" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361273 1145 "Writing a decoupled system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are parallel to the axes. These correspond to so-called straight-line solutions of the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The tangents along the $x$-axis are pointing away from the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}>0.$\n\n- The tangents along the $y$-axis are pointing toward the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nAmong the options, the only system that satisfies ${\\lambda }_{1}>0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}<0$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361275 13194139535688 true] [17592186361274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361276 13194139535688 true] [17592186361274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361277 13194139535688 true] [17592186361274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361278 13194139535688 true] [17592186361274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361279 13194139535688 true] [17592186361274 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535688 true] [17592186361274 1041 "selection" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361274 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361276 13194139535688 true] [17592186361274 1110 #uuid "0c8e1d3c-3117-5622-9513-219fc1a16376" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361275 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4y(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139535688 true] [17592186361275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535688 true] [17592186361275 1111 #uuid "c9a3cd4d-872c-5dbe-a775-d669a739a4b1" 13194139535688 true] [1759218636